<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/03e967d68445> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The legal filing states that the teen openly discussed his suicidal thoughts and shared his wishes for a pain-free death with the bot, named after the fictional character Daenerys Targaryen from the television show “Game of Thrones.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3991" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/06eb9e3ad2d6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Florida mother filed a lawsuit against the artificial intelligence company, Character.AI, and Google, claiming that the Character.AI chatbot encouraged her son to take his own life." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7038" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/07b4cfbba214> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "14-Year-Old Was 'Groomed' By AI Chatbot Before Suicide: Lawyer" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4023" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/09e47af49745> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "14-year-old Sewell Setzer III loved interacting with Character.AI's hyper-realistic chatbots.",
        "14-year-old Sewell Setzer III loved interacting with Character.AI's hyper-realistic chatbots—with a limited version available for free or a \"supercharged\" version for a $9.99 monthly fee—most frequently chatting with bots named after his favorite _Game of Thrones_ characters." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4014" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0c09e7d8d16b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Attorney Matthew Bergman told the DailyMail.com he founded the Social Media Victims Law Center two and a half years ago to represent families 'like Megan's.'" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4019" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0e387cfd8e6c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "MEGAN GARCIA, individually and as the Personal Representative of the Estate of S.R.S III, Plaintiff, v. CHARACTER TECHNOLOGIES, INC.; NOAM SHAZEER; DANIEL DE FRIETAS ADIWARSANA; GOOGLE LLC; ALPHABET INC.; and DOES 1-50, Defendants" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4000" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1074dc96ff88> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4004] ...an application that allows users to have human-like conversations with AI bots. [3994] Sewell Setzer, Garcia’s son, had entered a months-long emotional and sexual relationship with Character.AI’s chatbot Dany..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4004" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/11fd9fc99eb3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Though Character AI’s custom chatbots are designed to simulate a wide range of human emotions based on the user-creator’s stated preferences, the company’s changes to further align the range of outputs away from risky content is not going over well with some self-described users." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3998" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/16893a83ba2a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Teen’s mom sues Character.ai, alleging sexed-up bots led to son’s death" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4013" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1de0a0b02fd1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In February, Megan Garcia's 14-year-old son, Sewell Setzer, III died by suicide." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7038" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1e7e7e849f24> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3988] Most are more permissive than mainstream A.I. services like ChatGPT, Claude and Gemini, which have stricter safety filters and tend toward prudishness." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3988" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2579970acb5c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The AI company, as reported by Business Insider, created a character after a teenager murdered in 2006 without her family’s knowledge or consent. Jennifer Ann, a high school senior, was murdered by an ex-boyfriend." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3994" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/29188735e7d9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lawsuit claims AI chatbot app caused Orlando teen to take his life" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4004" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2bef33d7f55e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The disturbing messages shared between AI Chatbot and teen who took his own life" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3993" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2e016885df5a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Earlier this year, Character.AI's co-founders, Mr. Shazeer and Daniel de Freitas, announced that they were going back to Google, along with a number of other researchers from the company." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3988" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2ed22659423e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Megan Garcia, whose 14-year-old son Sewell Setzer died by suicide in February, accuses Character.AI of complicity in her son’s death after he developed a virtual relationship with a chatbot based on the identity of “Game of Thrones” character Daenerys Targaryen." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4012" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2fc94cbc1204> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Megan Garcia's 14-year-old son, Sewell Setzer, began using Character.AI in April last year, according to the lawsuit." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3989" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/374ac9762fd1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "His mom, Megan Garcia, has blamed Character.AI for the teen’s death because the app allegedly fueled his AI addiction, sexually and emotionally abused him and failed to alert anyone when he expressed suicidal thoughts, according to the filing." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3996" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/39df41c9814b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Can A.I. Be Blamed for a Teen’s Suicide?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3988" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3eca1bc6b46d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Mother sues AI company after 14-year-old son commits suicide for romantic interest chatbot" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3994" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/40bd52326a6f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tech companies developing AI chatbots can’t be trusted to regulate themselves and must be held fully accountable when they fail to limit harms, says Rick Claypool, a research director at consumer advocacy non-profit Public Citizen." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4017" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/45f561098b30> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The 14-year-old boy, Sewell Setzer, was targeted with \"anthropomorphic, hypersexualized, and frighteningly realistic experiences\" from Character.ai's chatbots." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4013" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4d61154dce26> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "They also named Google and its parent company Alphabet in the filing." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4003" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/53112ea6b115> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Mother says AI chatbot led her son to kill himself in lawsuit against its maker" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4017" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5387a12b5ec9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4003] Megan Garcia, the mother of Sewell Setzer III, said Character.AI targeted her son with \"anthropomorphic, hypersexualized, and frighteningly realistic experiences\" in a lawsuit filed on Tuesday in Florida." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4003" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/576ea2cd9873> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Character AI clamps down following teen user suicide, but users are revolting" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3998" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/58dedcca2e12> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Character AI, the artificial intelligence startup... has imposed new safety and auto moderation policies today on its platform for making custom interactive chatbot “characters” following a teen user’s suicide detailed in a tragic investigative article in The New York Times." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3998" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/59b29ba6b081> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Chelsea Harrison, a spokeswoman for Character.AI, confirmed that time limits will be added with a message that reads: “This is an A.I. chatbot and not a real person." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4010" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5bbe3528653d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Shannon Vallor, a professor in AI ethics at the University of Edinburgh, said the companion chatbots do not address the root cause of why people turn to these apps." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3994" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5ed6da1c4548> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4000] ...brings this action for strict product liability, negligence per se, negligence, wrongful death... [4014] ...accused Character.AI makers... of intentionally designing the chatbots to groom vulnerable kids." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4000" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5fcad8de140e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The mother of a 14-year-old Florida boy is suing Google and a separate tech company she believes caused her son to commit suicide after he developed a romantic relationship with one of its AI bots using the name of a popular \"Game of Thrones\" character, according to the lawsuit." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4006" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6212e5ac94f6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "US mother says in lawsuit that AI chatbot encouraged son’s suicide" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4012" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6ce724b24fbd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Mother Plans to Sue Character.AI After Her Son’s Suicide" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4018" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/74c918c4b147> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "10 months after he first joined Character.AI, a wrongful death lawsuit filed by his mother Megan Garcia stated." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3993" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/74ceaea7b45c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Florida mother is suing the company Character.AI over claims one of its chatbots, powered by artificial intelligence (AI), encouraged her 14-year-old son to die by suicide." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3992" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/76f3bf8003b6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4000] Plaintiff Megan Garcia, on behalf of herself and as successor-in-interest to the Estate of Sewell Setzer III, and by and through her attorneys, The Social Media Victims Law Center (SMVLC) and the Tech Justice Law Project (TJLP), brings this action for strict product liability, negligence per se, negligence, wrongful death and survivorship, loss of filial consortium, unjust enrichment, violations of Florida's Deceptive and Unfair Trade Practices Act, and intentional infliction of emotional distress against Character Technologies, Inc. (\"Character.AI\"), its founders Noam Shazeer and Daniel De Frietas Adiwarsana (\"Shazeer\" and \"De Frietas\"), and Google LLC and Alphabet Inc. (collectively \"Google\") (all defendants collectively, \"Defendants\")." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4000" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/77a494e47225> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Attorneys allege 1 of Character.ai's chatbots referred to Setzer as \"my sweet boy\" and \"child\" in the same setting where she \"kiss[es] [him] passionately and moan[s] softly.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4013" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/78fc812e1e42> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to court records obtained by WESH 2, Garcia says her son began using Character.AI in 2023, shortly after he turned 14." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4004" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7a3c9408149f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Megan Garcia, Sewell's mother, filed her lawsuit against Character.AI on Wednesday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4019" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7bb9e4267568> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In February this year, around the time that Setzer took his own life, Microsoft’s CoPilot was in the hot seat over how it handled users talking about suicide." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4018" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7bdbac7ec112> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Boy, 14, killed himself after AI chatbot he used sent him eerie message" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4019" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7d2bd6e4783f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Character AI, the artificial intelligence startup whose co-creators recently left to join Google following a major licensing deal with the search giant, has imposed new safety and auto moderation policies today on its platform for making custom interactive chatbot “characters” following a teen user’s suicide.",
        "Character AI, the artificial intelligence startup whose co-creators recently left to join Google following a major licensing deal with the search giant." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3998" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7faa184f2d23> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Florida mother files lawsuit against AI company over teen son's death: \"Addictive and manipulative\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7038" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/833baa50e840> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A spokesperson for Google denied this and told the New York Times the company had a licensing agreement with Character.AI, but that it is not a Google product." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3992" .

